            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 16 changed paths for security, data-loss and unsafe-input risk.",
              "The main risk change is in engine/review/fsstore/held_linux.go. It reports a post-link directory flush failure as app.ErrNotFlushed, wrapped with %w. engine/review/app/service.go treats that error as stored, so Record does not retry and does not write a second copy. The openat/O_NOFOLLOW/O_EXCL walk and the linkat publish are unchanged, so no new symlink-redirect or overwrite path is introduced.",
              "The new error wrapping of mkdir and open failures in held_linux.go only changes message text. Its ELOOP/ENOTDIR handling still routes symlink and non-directory cases to notADirectory, so the refusal of symlinks on the path is preserved.",
              "engine/review/fsstore/fsstore.go adds a syncDir test hook that is nil in New(), so it is not reachable in production. temporaryName builds names from tempPattern, so the names Names hides match the names the writer stages.",
              "engine/cmd/review.go reportRecorded prints the flush warning and still exits 0 with the handoff skeleton. A stdout write failure still exits 1 with the stored path in the message. No secrets or sensitive data are added to the output.",
              "engine/review/gitexec/gitexec.go: Worktree now builds its observer via g.observer(), which was not visible in this patch. That helper's environment handling is outside the candidate view and was not assessed. The rest of the change is a comment.",
              "The remaining changes are tests, fixtures, CHANGELOG and task documentation, with no runtime effect."
            ]
          }
        }
